## Diplomat Architecture — Layer Overview

Nubank services follow the **Diplomat Architecture**, a Hexagonal / Ports & Adapters variant with strict naming and layering conventions.

```
External world
     │
     ▼
diplomat.*          ← entry/exit points (HTTP server, Kafka consumer/producer, DB, HTTP client)
     │
adapters.*          ← pure functions: translate wire ↔ model
     │
controllers.*       ← orchestrate domain flows; call diplomat.* and logic.*
     │
logic.*             ← pure business logic; model-only deps, no side effects
     │
models.*            ← data shape definitions (plumatic/schema)
     │
wire.in / wire.out  ← external data contracts (inbound loose, outbound strict)
```

### Layer Dependency Rules

| Layer | May depend on |
|---|---|
| `diplomat.consumer` | `adapters`, `wire`, `controllers`, `models` |
| `diplomat.http-server` | `adapters`, `wire`, `controllers`, `models` |
| `diplomat.http-client` | `adapters`, `wire`, `models` |
| `diplomat.producer` | `adapters`, `wire`, `models` |
| `db.datomic.*` | `adapters`, `wire.datomic`, `models` |
| `adapters` | `wire`, `logic`, `models` — pure functions only |
| `wire.*` | `models` only |
| `models` | nothing — pure data structures |
| `controllers` | `db.datomic.*`, `diplomat.*`, `models`, `logic` — **never** imports adapters directly |
| `logic` | `models` only — **must** be pure (no side effects, no I/O) |

### Domain layer (concepts)

Canonical definitions follow Nubank’s [Diplomat Architecture Concepts — Domain layer](https://nubank.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGCHAP/pages/262706725402/Diplomat+Architecture+Concepts#Domain-Layer) (ENGCHAP / `#guild-code-quality`).

**Domain layer (scope)** — Implements the service’s purpose: core behavior and business rules. It coordinates work and may invoke **external layer** capabilities (HTTP clients, producers, databases, etc.) to observe or change system state. **Wire** schemas are not part of the domain layer; use **models** inside the domain and adapt at **diplomat** boundaries.

**Controller** — Orchestrates **one** domain flow, combining **domain** pieces (`logic`, `models`) with **external** capabilities (`diplomat.*`, `db.*`, protocol components). Controllers are usually **impure** (they depend on live system state and often perform side effects). They are **narrower than MVC controllers**: they do **not** own request parsing, response shaping, or wire schemas (that is **diplomat** + **adapters**), and they do **not** embed persistence mechanics (that stays in **database** modules the controller calls). **Do not call adapters from controllers** — wire ↔ model translation belongs in the **external layer** (e.g. HTTP handler, consumer handler, producer wrapper), not inside `controllers.*`. **Do not pass components** (e.g. `config`, database components) into **logic**; read the needed values in the controller and pass plain data (`models`, primitives) into logic so logic stays deterministic and cheap to unit test. In graph-style APIs (GraphQL, **pathom** BFFs, etc.), **resolvers** often act as controllers when they orchestrate external I/O and domain steps the same way.

**Logic** — Encodes **business rules** and **conditionals** for the domain. **Must be pure**: deterministic for the same arguments, **no side effects**, **no I/O**. **Must not call** diplomats, adapters, databases, HTTP/Kafka clients, or components — only **`logic.*`** and **`models.*`**. Favor **high unit test coverage** without mocks when these rules hold.

**Model** — Declares **domain data shapes** (entities and values the service reasons about). Models should be the **only** data structures used **inside the domain layer**. Prefer **strict** schemas. **Do not mirror database entity layout** in models — persistence shape lives under **`wire.datomic`** (or other wire DB namespaces); **adapters** convert model ↔ wire DB. **Adapters** also convert model ↔ **wire.in** / **wire.out** at boundaries; keep wire types out of business rules.

For exceptions vs domain errors and broader implementation detail, see [Diplomat Architecture Implementation Guidelines](https://nubank.atlassian.net/wiki/display/ENGCHAP/Diplomat+Architecture+Implementation+Guidelines) on Confluence.

