## Naming Conventions

### Files and Namespaces

- **Files**: `snake_case.clj`
- **Namespaces**: `service-name.layer.feature-name` (kebab-case), matching the file path

```clojure
;; file: src/better_call_saul/controllers/card_identify.clj
(ns better-call-saul.controllers.card-identify ...)

;; file: src/piata/wire/in/authorization.clj
(ns piata.wire.in.authorization ...)
```

### Require Aliases

Use `layer.feature` aliases to make the origin layer clear:

```clojure
(:require [better-call-saul.diplomat.http-client.card-skins :as http-client.card-skins]
          [better-call-saul.logic.card-summaries            :as logic.card-summaries]
          [better-call-saul.models.card-skin                :as models.card-skin]
          [better-call-saul.wire.in.card-identify           :as wire.in.card-identify]
          [better-call-saul.wire.out.card-identify          :as wire.out.card-identify])
```

### Schema Names

- Schemas: `PascalCase` (e.g., `CardSummary`, `IdentifyCardRequest`, `ProtoCard`)
- Skeletons (reusable maps): `^:private skeleton` (kebab-case symbol)

### Functions

- All functions: `kebab-case`
- Side-effecting functions (I/O, DB, Kafka): suffix with `!` (e.g., `lookup!`, `upsert!`, `customer-name!`)
- Pure functions: no `!` suffix

### Adapter Function Naming

| Direction | Naming |
|---|---|
| Inbound wire → model | `wire->model` |
| Model → outbound wire | `model->wire` |
| Datomic entity → model | `datomic->internal` or `datomic->model` |
| Model → Datomic entity | `internal->datomic` or `model->datomic` |

