## Schema Patterns

### wire.in — Loose (tolerant reader)

```clojure
(ns better-call-saul.wire.in.card-identify
  (:require [common-core.schema :as schema]
            [schema.core :as s]))

(def ^:private skeleton
  {:proto-card-id {:schema s/Uuid :required false}
   :pan-encrypted {:schema s/Str  :required false :sensitive true}})

(s/defschema IdentifyCardRequest
  (schema/loose-schema skeleton))
```

### wire.out — Strict (conservative publisher)

```clojure
(ns better-call-saul.wire.out.card-identify
  (:require [common-core.schema :as schema]
            [schema.core :as s]))

(s/defschema ProtoCard
  (schema/strict-schema
   {:proto-card-id {:schema s/Uuid :required true}
    :pan-last-four {:schema s/Str  :required false}}))
```

### models — Strict domain types

```clojure
(ns better-call-saul.models.card-identify
  (:require [common-core.schema :as schema]
            [schema.core :as s]))

(s/defschema IdentifyRequest
  (schema/strict-schema
   {:proto-card-id {:schema s/Uuid :required false}
    :pan-encrypted {:schema s/Str  :required false}}))
```

### wire.datomic — Strict, namespaced keywords

DB schemas live in `wire/datomic/<entity>.clj`. They use **namespaced map literals** (`#:ns{}`), always `strict-schema`, and include DB metadata (`:id true`, `:doc`, `:index`). **Never reuse models as wire.datomic** — they are separate schemas adapted in both directions.

```clojure
;; wire/datomic/card_skin.clj
(ns better-call-saul.wire.datomic.card-skin
  (:require [common-core.schema :as schema]
            [schema.core :as s]))

;; Persisted = what comes back from a query (includes DB attrs, may be optional)
(def ^:private skeleton
  #:card-skin{:id           {:schema s/Uuid :id true    :doc "Card skin selection ID"}
              :card-id      {:schema s/Uuid :index true  :doc "Associated card ID"}
              :skin-id      {:schema s/Str               :doc "Selected skin identifier"}
              :collection-id {:schema s/Str              :doc "Skin collection"}
              :customer-id  {:schema s/Uuid :index true  :doc "Owner customer ID"}
              :selected-at  {:schema s/Inst :required false :doc "Selection timestamp"}})

(s/defschema Persisted
  (schema/strict-schema skeleton))
```

