## Testing

### Unit Tests (logic and adapters only)

```clojure
;; test/unit/better_call_saul/adapters/card_identify_test.clj
(ns better-call-saul.adapters.card-identify-test
  (:require [better-call-saul.adapters.card-identify :as adapters.card-identify]
            [clojure.test :refer :all]
            [clojure.test.check.clojure-test :refer [defspec]]
            [common-test.schema :as schema-test]))

(defspec wire->model-round-trip 50
  (schema-test/for-all [wire (schema-test/generator wire.in.card-identify/IdentifyCardRequest)]
    (is (= (adapters.card-identify/wire->model wire)
           (adapters.card-identify/wire->model wire)))))
```

- **Only pure function namespaces get unit tests**: `logic.*` and `adapters.*`
- `diplomat.*` (http-client, http-server, consumer, producer) and `controllers.*` are **excluded** from unit tests — even if a specific namespace test wouldn't be "wrong", the team does not maintain them
- Logic and adapters should have **high unit test coverage**

### Integration Tests (state-flow)

```clojure
;; test/integration/integration/card_identify_test.clj
(ns integration.card-identify-test
  (:require [integration.aux.request :as request]
            [integration.aux.non-perso-card :as stubs.non-perso-card]
