## Datomic / DB Layer

### Directory and Namespace

```
src/<service>/db/datomic/<entity>.clj
→ ns: <service>.db.datomic.<entity>
```

Examples:
```clojure
;; src/fina_estampa/db/datomic/country.clj
(ns fina-estampa.db.datomic.country ...)

;; src/better_call_saul/db/datomic/card_skin.clj
(ns better-call-saul.db.datomic.card-skin ...)
```

### Datomic Adapters

DB-specific adapters live in the same `adapters/` directory as other adapters. If adapters grow large, they can live in a sub-file named after the entity.

```clojure
;; adapters/card_skin.clj
(ns better-call-saul.adapters.card-skin
  (:require [better-call-saul.models.card-skin        :as models.card-skin]
            [better-call-saul.wire.datomic.card-skin  :as wire.datomic.card-skin]
            [schema.core :as s]))

(s/defn internal->datomic :- wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted
  [{:keys [id card-id skin-id collection-id customer-id selected-at]}
   :- models.card-skin/CardSkin]
  #:card-skin{:id            id
              :card-id       card-id
              :skin-id       skin-id
              :collection-id collection-id
              :customer-id   customer-id
              :selected-at   selected-at})

(s/defn datomic->internal :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
  [{:card-skin/keys [id card-id skin-id collection-id customer-id selected-at]}
   :- wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted]
  {:id            id
   :card-id       card-id
   :skin-id       skin-id
   :collection-id collection-id
   :customer-id   customer-id
   :selected-at   selected-at})
```

### DB Function Pattern

```clojure
;; db/datomic/card_skin.clj
(ns better-call-saul.db.datomic.card-skin
  (:require [better-call-saul.adapters.card-skin          :as adapters.card-skin]
            [better-call-saul.models.card-skin             :as models.card-skin]
            [better-call-saul.wire.datomic.card-skin       :as wire.datomic.card-skin]
            [common-core.schema                            :as core.schema]
            [common-datomic.api                            :as db]
            [common-datomic.db                             :as ddb]
            [common-datomic.protocols.datomic              :as protocols.datomic]
            [schema.core                                   :as s])
  (:import [datomic.db Db]))

;; Reads receive a DB value (Db snapshot), not the datomic component
(s/defn lookup! :- (s/maybe models.card-skin/CardSkin)
  [card-id :- s/Uuid
   db      :- Db]
  (some-> (db/lookup [:card-skin/card-id card-id] db)
          (core.schema/loose-coerce! wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted)
          adapters.card-skin/datomic->internal))

;; Batch queries return collections
(s/defn fetch-by-card-ids! :- [models.card-skin/CardSkin]
  [card-ids :- [s/Uuid]
   db       :- Db]
  (let [result (db/entities '{:find  [?e]
                               :in    [$ [?card-id ...]]
                               :where [[?e :card-skin/card-id ?card-id]]}
                             db card-ids)]
    (->> (core.schema/loose-coerce! result [wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted])
         (mapv adapters.card-skin/datomic->internal))))

;; Writes receive the datomic component
(s/defn upsert! :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
  [skin    :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
   datomic :- protocols.datomic/IDatomic]
  (-> (adapters.card-skin/internal->datomic skin)
      (db/upsert-entity! :card-skin/id datomic)  ;; note: first arg is datomic entity map
      :entity
      (core.schema/loose-coerce! wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted)
      adapters.card-skin/datomic->internal))

;; Insert (unique constraint — throws on duplicate)
(s/defn create! :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
  [skin    :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
   datomic :- protocols.datomic/IDatomic]
  (-> (adapters.card-skin/internal->datomic skin)
      (db/insert-entity! :card-skin/id datomic)
      :entity
      (core.schema/loose-coerce! wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted)
      adapters.card-skin/datomic->internal))

;; Retraction
(s/defn retract!
  [id      :- s/Uuid
   datomic :- protocols.datomic/IDatomic]
  (db/retract-entity! [:card-skin/id id] datomic))
```

### Controller Using DB Layer

```clojure
;; controllers/card_skins.clj
(ns better-call-saul.controllers.card-skins
  (:require [better-call-saul.db.datomic.card-skin    :as db.card-skin]
            [better-call-saul.logic.card-skins         :as logic.card-skins]
            [better-call-saul.models.card-skin         :as models.card-skin]
            [common-datomic.db                         :as ddb]
            [common-datomic.protocols.datomic          :as protocols.datomic]
            [schema.core                               :as s]))

;; Get the DB snapshot once; reuse it for all reads in the same flow
(s/defn get-card-skin! :- (s/maybe models.card-skin/CardSkin)
  [card-id :- s/Uuid
   datomic :- protocols.datomic/IDatomic]
  (let [db (ddb/db datomic)]
    (db.card-skin/lookup! card-id db)))

(s/defn upsert-card-skin! :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
  [skin    :- models.card-skin/CardSkin
   datomic :- protocols.datomic/IDatomic]
  (let [validated (logic.card-skins/validate! skin)]
    (db.card-skin/upsert! validated datomic)))
```

### DB Integration Test Helpers

State-flow integration tests seed and query Datomic through helpers in `aux/db/`:

```clojure
;; test/integration/integration/aux/db/card_skin.clj
(ns integration.aux.db.card-skin
  (:require [better-call-saul.wire.datomic.card-skin :as wire.datomic.card-skin]
            [common-datomic.api                      :as db]
            [schema.core                             :as s]
            [state-flow.helpers.core                 :as helpers]))

(s/defn upsert!
  [skin :- wire.datomic.card-skin/Persisted]
  (helpers/with-datomic #(db/upsert-entity! :card-skin/id skin %)))

(s/defn fetch-all []
  (helpers/with-db
    #(db/entities '{:find  [?e]
                    :where [[?e :card-skin/id _]]} %)))
```

### Key Datomic Rules

- **Read functions take `Db` (snapshot), write functions take the `datomic` component** — never mix them.
- **Get one snapshot per controller flow**: call `(ddb/db datomic)` once and pass it to all read functions in the same flow. Calling it multiple times yields different snapshots.
- **Never reuse models as wire.datomic** — they are separate schemas. Models have plain keywords; wire.datomic uses namespaced keywords (`#:entity{}`).
- **Always adapt before writing** (`internal->datomic`) and after reading (`datomic->internal`). DB functions own these adapter calls — controllers do not.
- **`common-core.schema/loose-coerce!`** is used to coerce raw Datomic results into the `wire.datomic` schema before adapting to model.
- **`:id true` marks the identity attribute** used as the lookup ref (e.g., `[:card-skin/id uuid]`).
- **`:index true`** on attributes queried in `:where` clauses for performance.
- **Do not store PII in cardinality-many attributes.**
- **Use `db/retract-entity!` with the lookup ref** (`[:entity/id uuid]`), not the numeric entity id.

